13v1)\nciteturn2731view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.00413v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 1 Oct 2025 (this version), latest version 4 Oct 2025 (cite5†v2 )]\nL9: # Title:PAL-UI: Planning with Active Look-back for Vision-Based GUI Agents\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Zikang Liu , cite7†Junyi Li , cite8†Wayne Xin Zhao , cite9†Dawei Gao , cite10†Yaliang Li , cite11†Ji-rong Wen L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled PAL-UI: Planning with Active Look-back for Vision-Based GUI Agents, by Zikang Liu and 5 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite12†View PDF cite13†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Graphical User Interface (GUI) agents powered by Multimodal Large Language Models (MLLMs) promise human-like interaction with software applications, yet long-horizon tasks remain challenging due to memory limitations. Existing approaches either truncate history or rely on simple textual summaries, which risk losing critical information when past visual details become necessary for future decisions.\nL17: In this paper, we propose \\textbf{PAL-UI} (\\textbf{P}lanning with \\textbf{A}ctive \\textbf{L}ook-back), a novel framework that enables GUI agents to adaptively retrieve past observations when required. PAL-UI combines a dual-level summarization agent, capturing both observation-level cues and action-level outcomes, with a dedicated retrieval tool that allows the agent to recall specific historical screenshots during planning.\nL18: We curate a step-level instruction dataset of 8.6K samples from mobile GUI navigation trajectories and train \\textbf{PAL-UI-3B} and \\textbf{PAL-UI-7B} models based on Qwen2.5-VL. Extensive experiments demonstrate that PAL-UI significantly outperforms baseline models and prior methods in mobile GUI navigation tasks, even under data-efficient settings. Moreover, PAL-UI exhibits strong cross-domain generalization, achieving notable improvements in web navigation without additional training.\nL19: Our work highlights the potential of active memory retrieval for long-horizon planning capabilities of vision-based GUI agents.\nL20: Subjects:  | Computer Vision and Pattern Recognition (cs.CV)\nL21: Cite as:  | cite14†arXiv:2510.00413 [cs.CV]\nL22:    | (or cite15†arXiv:2510.00413v1 [cs.CV] for this version)\nL23:    | cite16†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2510.00413†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Zikang Liu [cite17†view email ]\nL27: [v1] Wed, 1 Oct 2025 01:48:39 UTC (280 KB)\nL28: cite5†[v2] Sat, 4 Oct 2025 15:23:55 UTC (280 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled PAL-UI: Planning with Active Look-back for Vision-Based GUI Agents, by Zikang Liu and 5 other authors\nL35: \nL36:   * cite12†View PDF L37:   * cite13†HTML (experimental) L38:   * cite18†TeX Source L39: \nL40: cite19†view license L41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: cs.CV\nL44: \nL45: cite20†< prev |   cite21†next > L46: \nL47: cite22†new | cite23†recent | cite24†2025-10 L48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: cite25†cs L52: \nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * cite26†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu L56:   * cite27†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com L57:   * cite28†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org L58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL